<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine govt sees Nov tax collection at $3.8 bln.</title>
<headline>Argentine govt sees Nov tax collection at $3.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's tax revenue will be around $3.8 billion in November, up from $3.5 billion in November 1995 and $3.7 billion in October, a senior government official said Friday.</p>
<p>The expected rise is due mostly to an increase in fuel levies, Tax Policy Undersecretary Guillermo Rodriguez Use told reporters.</p>
<p>He said a &quot;conservative&quot; estimate was putting December tax collection a little below November's.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Adam, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 54 1 318-0654</p>
